omitted) in place of a declarator (9.3.4.6, 14.1), it is as if a unique identifier were included in the appropriate
place (9.3.2). The preceding specifiers indicate the type, storage class or other properties of the entity or
entities being declared. Each declarator specifies one entity and (optionally) names it and/or modifies the
type of the specifiers with operators such as * (pointer to) and () (function returning).
[Note 1: An init-declarator can also specify an initializer (9.4). — end note]
