The declarator shall correspond to one or more declarations found by the lookup; they shall all
have the same target scope, and the target scope of the declarator is that scope.
—
(2.3)
Otherwise, the terminal name of E is not looked up. The declaration’s target scope is the innermost
enclosing namespace scope; if the declaration is contained by a block scope, the declaration shall
correspond to a reachable (10.7) declaration that inhabits the innermost block scope.
3 Otherwise:
