(3.3)
If the declarator declares an explicit instantiation or a partial or explicit specialization, the declarator
does not bind a name. If it declares a class member, the terminal name of the declarator-id is not looked
up; otherwise, only those lookup results that are nominable in S are considered when identifying any
function template specialization being declared (13.10.3.7).
