A call to an atomic waiting operation on an atomic object M is eligible to be unblocked by a call to an atomic
notifying operation on M if there exist side effects X and Y on M such that:
—
(4.1)
the atomic waiting operation has blocked after observing the result of X,
—
(4.2)
X precedes Y in the modification order of M, and
—
(4.3)
Y happens before the call to the atomic notifying operation.
